    <briefdescription>
<para>Interning collection that pairs a <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_set_fixed_size" kindref="compound">MonomialSetFixedSize</ref></computeroutput> with its own <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_memory_space" kindref="compound">MonomialMemorySpace</ref></computeroutput> to own monomial storage. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput>findOrInsert(monom)</computeroutput> copies the caller&apos;s monomial into the arena, tries to insert the new pointer into the set, and pops the allocation back off the arena if a duplicate was already present (the &quot;intern-or-pop&quot; pattern). <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_collection_fixed_size_adad51c1e22168ba6f29e9dabee8e1d6f_1adad51c1e22168ba6f29e9dabee8e1d6f" kindref="member">monomialMemorySpace()</ref></computeroutput> exposes the arena so callers that allocate first and then insert can do so without an extra copy. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
